{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"198ee5d06128616568f8c6e87d75f04374edd3f6e3ffe58abe80fd58ef6a93e3","occurred_at":"2026-11-09T19:17:38Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_recovered_from":"c850eb5c5b58bb2f2eb53fca6c8f5406e2631677caf33654fd34b7ba11798338","anchor_verified":true,"mapped_intervals":[[298,298]],"mapped_path":"src/ops/dev/denylist.ts","quoted_text":"  const lines = text.split('\\n');","reason":"At the pinned tip, `scanText` still splits input only on `'\\n'` (line 298), so CRLF content leaves a trailing `\\r` on each scanned line. In JavaScript, `.` does not match `\\r` and `$` without the `m` flag matches only input end, so an end-anchored rule such as `token=.*$` cannot match `token=abc\\r`. This is an implementation defect in the fail-closed denylist scan, not a new requirement; the proposed `\\r?\\n` split preserves 1-based line numbering.","recovered_anchor":{"anchor_recovered_from":"c850eb5c5b58bb2f2eb53fca6c8f5406e2631677caf33654fd34b7ba11798338","blob":"60178b44c8cec37136530bb1f702e3e3ef91e6bc","intervals":[[298,298]],"path":"src/ops/dev/denylist.ts"},"target":"86247bb624de9ef20453df5d66ce9ef84040f933"},"finding_id":"cb5f3b885a6654a890d8ed1ff8a5ddacfa04076fdf4117e14925b17e1001919e","previous_event_id":null,"review_id":"e9cafb420b3650ac8dec65277650f938f997d2d266c93becb6f5c806ce8da4e5"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:cb5f3b885a6654a890d8ed1ff8a5ddacfa04076fdf4117e14925b17e1001919e:b40c7a7ca588dc8b7fd9fb8fe171d08f0a473dbb64518f2d9d0eacc4639bed68"}